    <entry>
        <title>My First Job</title>
        <author>
            <name>Kevin Kwilinski</name>
        </author>
        <link href="https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/my-deaf-mom.html"/>
        <id>https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/my-deaf-mom.html</id>
        <media:content url="https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/media/posts/24/signlanguage.jpg" medium="image" />

        <updated>2026-09-28T21:13:36-04:00</updated>
            <summary type="html">
                <![CDATA[
                        <img src="https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/media/posts/24/signlanguage.jpg" alt="" />
                    She lived her life with an immature desire. Dancing and singing, her&hellip;
                ]]>
            </summary>
        <content type="html">
            <![CDATA[
                    <p><img src="https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/media/posts/24/signlanguage.jpg" class="type:primaryImage" alt="" /></p>
                <div class="align-center">She lived her life with an immature desire.<br>Dancing and singing, her face lit a room.<br>But like a firecracker before the boom,<br>many often held their breath while by her.</div>
<div class="align-center"> </div>
<div class="align-center">I remember once, while near that line of fire,<br>I blushed, a boy of five, from her strong fume.<br>Her lips spewing forth in an obscene plume,<br>while she alone would not hear the deafening ire.</div>
<div class="align-center"> </div>
<div class="align-center">Then I’d relay the circumspect reply,<br>from a confused face speaking through her child,<br>as my mother lit a fresh cigarette.</div>
<div class="align-center"> </div>
<div class="align-center">Rewinding the tape with her careful eye,<br>she watched me imitate the words which riled,<br>never showing me a small sign of regret.</div>
            ]]>
        </content>
    </entry>
